title: Your next test
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder told you in person: your Tier 3 test is Monday at 09:00, a junction shutdown on Deck 6. Pass it and you're a Senior Officer.
== lines
calder > you: Stop a minute. This is the good kind.   [gesture]
calder: Relied on, as of today. Power safety, done. Nothing left.
calder: Monday. Your next test. Tier 3. Nine o'clock, on the board.
calder: Deck 6, a power junction. Off, a new breaker, back on. Nobody hurt, nobody surprised.
? choice
* Monday. I'll be ready.   rel:calder+2
  calder: I know. Rest this weekend. Properly. That's not a suggestion.   [nod]
* Switching power off? On purpose?   rel:calder+2
  calder: On purpose. Planned, warned, timed. That's the difference between a shutdown and a fault.   [nod]
calder: Pass it and you're a Senior Officer. Enjoy your weekend.
